{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Spun from 73d8 (brainy-convulsant-unicorn) and 551b (sanidine-cilium-eland) during the 2026-08-30 error-code decision pass.\n\n## Problem\n`error_code_for` (`src/rebar/_errors.py`) maps the broad `LLMError` family to `llm_unavailable`. That over-claims an AI-provider outage for non-outage faults: the bare `LLMError` base, bare/non-outage `WorkflowError` cases, and concrete LLM/workflow subclasses that are not in the provider-unavailability subtree. This is the residual of origin 8a31's blanket mapping and the systematic completion of epic 3405's descriptiveness intent.\n\n## Operator decision\nLatest DECISION NEEDED comment approves narrowing `llm_unavailable` to true outages only. The classifier keeps `isinstance(exc, LLMUnavailableError) -> llm_unavailable`, which intentionally includes the existing availability/config subtree (`LLMConfigError`, prompt/reviewer config errors) because those classes already model missing LLM dependencies/credentials/config as unavailability. The classifier must remove the broad `isinstance(exc, LLMError) -> llm_unavailable` catch-all so bare `LLMError` and non-availability subclasses no longer claim an outage.\n\nPreserve dbca AC3 for genuine execute-step outages: a bare `WorkflowError` that is the execute-step outage wrapper (current contract uses the `execute step failed:` message form) still maps to `llm_unavailable`. A bare `WorkflowError` without that execute-outage form, including the missing-bundle case from `src/rebar/llm/workflow/editor.py:475`, maps to `command_failed`. Do not add `environment_unready`.\n\n73d8 is folded into this sweep by giving `ExpressionError` an explicit `error_code = \"invalid_input\"`, matching prior bug 35ab (unknown-step -> invalid_input) and dbca (parse/lint -> invalid_input).\n\n## Implementation scope\nTouch `src/rebar/_errors.py`, `src/rebar/llm/workflow/executor.py`, and tests. Enumerate every concrete subclass of `LLMError` across `src/rebar/llm/`, including `errors.py`, `findings.py`, `evals/eval.py`, `prompting/`, and `workflow/`, with Serena hierarchy/reference checks and a grep/string confirmation. Intended mapping: `LLMUnavailableError` and its availability/config subtree -> `llm_unavailable`; the bare `WorkflowError` execute-step outage wrapper -> `llm_unavailable`; `ExpressionError` -> `invalid_input`; workflow caller/authoring errors already classified as `invalid_input` stay there; every remaining LLM/prompt-independent/findings/eval/snapshot subclass without an explicit `error_code` -> `command_failed`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `src/rebar/_errors.py` returns `llm_unavailable` for `LLMUnavailableError`/`LLMConfigError` availability errors and for the bare `WorkflowError` execute-step outage wrapper; a focused test verifies a genuine execute-step outage wrapper still maps to `llm_unavailable`.\n- [ ] The broad `LLMError` base and every non-availability `LLMError` subclass not classified by an earlier workflow-caller or availability branch maps to an explicit `error_code` when present, otherwise `command_failed`; a parameterized taxonomy test covers the complete enumerated subclass set.\n- [ ] `ExpressionError` maps to `invalid_input` via an explicit `error_code`, verified by a focused test and by the exhaustive taxonomy test.\n- [ ] The editor missing-bundle `WorkflowError` from `src/rebar/llm/workflow/editor.py:475` maps to `command_failed`, not `llm_unavailable`, verified by a focused test.\n- [ ] No `environment_unready` code is introduced; `KNOWN_ERROR_CODES` remains consistent with the intentional taxonomy.\n\n## Testing\nRun `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest -q` on the focused error-taxonomy tests added/updated for this change, plus `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint` and `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make typecheck`. Before push, run `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" rebar verify-commit-ticket HEAD` after committing."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788294716427757239,"uuid":"ecb23fbb-fd00-4418-8e62-3834b1366b48"}